# Round anniversaries (25, 50, 75, 100, 150, 200, 250, 300, then every 100 years) of big events only.
# An event is big when a state holiday or significant day commemorates it (state-days.neon), or when
# its own article – the primary article, or else the first linked article that qualifies – is itself
# an event of one of these types (Wikidata P31/P279*), dated (P585, P580 or P571) in the year of the
# event, with at least minSitelinks language editions (by section: Czech events have fewer).
# Not the general „document“ (Q49848): through its subclasses it covers websites, software and award
# ceremonies (Wikipedia, MediaWiki, the Oscars); the specific types of documents below stay.
# Reasons for the classes and the thresholds: docs/rozhodnuti.md.
parameters:
	anniversaries:
		minSitelinks:
			world: 60   # upper quartile of the 587 event articles whose date matches their event (median 37)
			cz: 15      # Czech events are written about in fewer languages (Charta 77: 36)
		eventClasses:
			Q198: válka
			Q10931: revoluce
			Q178561: bitva
			Q124734: povstání
			Q1168287: intervence
			Q645883: vojenská operace
			Q18603729: zánik státu nebo územního celku
			Q1464916: vyhlášení nezávislosti
			Q625298: mírová smlouva
			Q752783: let člověka do vesmíru
			Q3839081: katastrofa
			Q13418847: historická událost
			Q131569: smlouva
			Q62662439: deklarace
			Q46337: manifest
			Q697279: petice
			Q206021: let
			Q2401485: expedice
